# Keep Functions Focused

## When adding or editing code

1. Give each function a clear responsibility and a name that describes it.
2. Separate complex steps when doing so makes behavior easier to understand or test.
3. Reuse an existing helper when it fits; remove duplicated logic introduced by the change.
4. Keep data flow and side effects visible.
5. Prefer straightforward code over extra layers for a single use case.

Do not split code into tiny wrappers just to satisfy a line count. Do not rewrite working functions outside the approved scope. If a larger refactor is needed to make the requested change safe, explain its impact before expanding the work.
